<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves via system RPs Thursday.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves via system RPs Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to inject reserves into the banking system via a round of term system repurchase agreements Thursday during its usual midmorning intervention period, economists said.</p>
<p>Fed funds opened at 5-3/8 percent and were trading at that level, slightly above the Fed's official target of 5-1/4 percent.</p>
<p>((--John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1663))</p>
